WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.572
Lang Chain is useful because it gives us common interfaces for many A I application components.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:10.282
You can absolutely build everything with normal Python.

00:00:10.282 --> 00:00:18.282
But as a project grows, you may have one model library, another vector database library, a document loader,

00:00:18.282 --> 00:00:21.882
several tools, and different prompt formats.

00:00:21.882 --> 00:00:27.158
Without a common interface, you often write adapter code between all of them.

00:00:27.618 --> 00:00:30.925
Lang Chain standardizes many of those connections.

00:00:30.925 --> 00:00:34.610
A document can be represented with a Document object.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.435
A retriever often supports invoke.

00:00:37.435 --> 00:00:41.145
Tools have names, descriptions, and schemas.

00:00:41.145 --> 00:00:43.995
Chat models use message objects.

00:00:43.995 --> 00:00:49.825
This makes it easier to replace one component without redesigning the whole application.

00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:57.850
For example, if your controller expects a retriever, you may be able to switch from an in-memory vector store to Chroma

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.573
without changing the high-level control logic.

00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:05.006
Lang Chain is optional. Learn the architecture first.

00:01:05.006 --> 00:01:11.344
Use the library because it reduces integration work, not because the project must contain a framework.
